{
  "opening": "This release introduces several enhancements to existing functions and adds new capabilities for sampling, permutation generation, and set partitioning. The changes focus on improving flexibility in iteration patterns and providing more precise control over data transformation and selection.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The `map_if` function must apply a specified transformation to items in an iterable based on a given condition, returning a new iterable with the mapped values. The `sample` function must support improved documentation or behavior regarding its sampling logic, ensuring consistent output formats."
    },
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "The `distinct_permutations` function must generate unique permutations of an iterable, handling incomparable items correctly without raising errors. The `permuted_items` function must yield permuted versions of items while maintaining distinctness constraints."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "The `seekable` wrapper must adjust its relative seeking behavior to accurately position the underlying iterable based on signed offsets from the current position."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "The `sample` function must accept a `counts` parameter to specify the number of samples to draw, returning a list of selected items. The `feed` and `is_sorted` functions must maintain their existing behaviors while supporting integration with the updated sampling logic."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "The `circular_shifts` function must accept a `steps` argument to define the shift amount, yielding iterables rotated by that many positions. The `exactly_n` and `run_length` functions must continue to operate as before, unaffected by the new `steps` parameter."
    },
    {
      "id": "m17",
      "text": "The `partitions` and `set_partitions` functions must expose parameters to specify minimum and maximum sizes for generated partitions, filtering results accordingly. The `replace` and `set_partitions_helper` functions must support these size constraints internally while preserving public API compatibility."
    },
    {
      "id": "m23",
      "text": "The `sort_together` function must accept a `strict` boolean argument; when True, it raises an error if input iterables have differing lengths. The `zip_offset` function must remain unchanged in behavior, continuing to zip iterables with specified offsets."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names are exposed exactly as listed and that observable behaviors match the descriptions above. Verify that no regressions occur in existing functionality while integrating these updates."
}
